		"nodes": {
			"1": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "PACK\nThis node packs multiple float inputs togehter to make a Float2, Float3 or Float4. To reverse this, the unpack node can be used. The size of the pack node is set in the inspector to either 2, 3 or 4.\n\n- Patch Explained -\n\n• The Sine generates values from -1 to 1. This gets packed together with the -0.75 value into a Float2 signal to modulate the Point A parameter of the Triangle\n• Three Float sliders (from 0 to 1) are packed into a Float 4 signal to adust the color of the shape. When used like this X contains red, Y contains green, Z contains blue and W contains the alpha."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 248.732879638671875,
					"width": 695,
					"x": 110.1156768798828125,
					"y": -91.0650482177734375
